<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!-- From "Medieval Horse Plate Armour" by Riful. Riful drew seven saddled-horse overlays
       for Giddy-Up so that a ridden horse shows tack under its rider; this points Giddy-Up at
       them.

       Two things had to change or it would silently do nothing:

       1. The class moved. Riful wrote GiddyUpCore.CompProperties_Overlay. In Giddy-Up 2 the
          type is GiddyUp.CompProperties_Overlay - same assembly name, GiddyUpCore.dll, but a
          different namespace. An unresolvable Class= on a <li> makes RimWorld discard the
          whole def it appears in, so this is not a cosmetic detail.

       2. The gate moved. Riful used PatchOperationFindMod with <li>Giddy-Up! Core</li>, which
          matches on a mod's DISPLAY NAME. The living mod is called "Giddy-Up 2 - Continued",
          so that test can never pass again. The folder is gated on the packageId
          MemeGoddess.GiddyUp in LoadFolders.xml instead, which does not depend on what the
          author calls the mod this month.

       The PatchOperationRemove is kept and still carries success Always: Giddy-Up may or may
       not already have given the horse an overlay comp, and either is fine.

       offsetDefault was (0,0,0,0) in the original. The field is a Vector3, so a four-component
       value does not parse; it is (0,0,0) here. -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationRemove">
    <success>Always</success>
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Horse"]/comps/li[@Class="GiddyUp.CompProperties_Overlay"]</xpath>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Horse"]/comps</xpath>
    <value>
      <li Class="GiddyUp.CompProperties_Overlay">
        <overlayFront>
          <graphicDataDefault>
            <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
            <drawSize>2.1</drawSize>
            <drawRotated>false</drawRotated>
          </graphicDataDefault>
          <allVariants>
            <li>
              <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Apparel/Overlay/Horse_overlay_south</texPath>
            </li>
            <li>
              <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Apparel/Overlay/Horse1_overlay_south</texPath>
            </li>
            <li>
              <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Apparel/Overlay/Horse2_overlay_south</texPath>
            </li>
            <li>
              <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Apparel/Overlay/Horse3_overlay_south</texPath>
            </li>
            <li>
              <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Apparel/Overlay/Horse4_overlay_south</texPath>
            </li>
            <li>
              <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Apparel/Overlay/Horse5_overlay_south</texPath>
            </li>
            <li>
              <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Apparel/Overlay/Horse6_overlay_south</texPath>
            </li>
          </allVariants>
          <offsetDefault>(0,0,0)</offsetDefault>
        </overlayFront>
      </li>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
